\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab At the end of the session, the students should be able to:\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 1. Enumerate the different controls in VB.Net\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 2. Explain how to use different Dialog Controls\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 3. Demonstrate Manipulation, Formatting, Methods, Advanced Editing, Cutting, Copying and Pasting Features in VB.Net\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 4. Describe the uses of Tree View and List View Controls\par
\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 3\par
\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 VB.Net - Dialog Boxes\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab There are many built-in dialog boxes to be used in Windows forms for various tasks like opening and saving files, printing a page, providing choices for colors, fonts, page setup, etc., to the user of an application. These built-in dialog boxes reduce the developer's time and workload.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab All of these dialog box control classes inherit from the CommonDialog class and override the RunDialog() function of the base class to create the specific dialog box.\par
\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 4\par
\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 VB.Net - Dialog Boxes (cont.)\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab The RunDialog() function is automatically invoked when a user of a dialog box calls its ShowDialog()function.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab The ShowDialog method is used to display all the dialog box controls at run-time. It returns a value of the type of DialogResult enumeration. The values of DialogResult enumeration are:\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Abort - returns DialogResult.Abort value, when user clicks an Abort button.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Cancel- returns DialogResult.Cancel, when user clicks a Cancel button.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Ignore - returns DialogResult.Ignore, when user clicks an Ignore button.\par
\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 5\par
\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 VB.Net - Dialog Boxes (cont.)\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab No - returns DialogResult.No, when user clicks a No button.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab None - returns nothing and the dialog box continues running.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab OK - returns DialogResult.OK, when user clicks an OK button\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Retry - returns DialogResult.Retry , when user clicks an Retry button\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Yes - returns DialogResult.Yes, when user clicks an Yes button\par
