\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab All these above-mentioned classes have corresponding controls that could be added from the Toolbox during design time. You can include relevant functionality of these classes to your application, either by instantiating the class programmatically or by using relevant controls.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab When you double click any of the dialog controls in the toolbox or drag the control onto the form, it appears in the Component tray at the bottom of the Windows Forms Designer, they do not directly show up on the form.\par
\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 8\par
\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 The following diagram shows the common dialog class inheritance: (cont.)\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab The following table lists the commonly used dialog box controls. Click the following links to check their detail:\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab S.N. Control & Description\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 1. ColorDialog\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab It represents a common dialog box that displays available colors along with controls that enable the user to define custom colors.\par
\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 9\par
\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 The following diagram shows the common dialog class inheritance: (cont.)\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 2.  FontDialog\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab It prompts the user to choose a font from among those installed on the local computer and lets the user select the font, font size, and color.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 3.  OpenFileDialog\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab It prompts the user to open a file and allows the user to select a file to open.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 4.  SaveFileDialog\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab It prompts the user to select a location for saving a file and allows the user to specify the name of the file to save data.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 5.  PrintDialog\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab It lets the user to print documents by selecting a printer and choosing which sections of the document to print from a Windows Forms application.\par
\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 10\par
\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 VB.Net - ColorDialog Control\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab The ColorDialog control class represents a common dialog box that displays available colors along with controls that enable the user to define custom colors. It lets the user select a color.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab The main property of the ColorDialog control is Color, which returns a Color object.\par
\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 11\par
