\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 18\par
\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 Properties of the FontDialog Control\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab The following are some of the commonly used properties of the FontDialog control:\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab S.N Property Description\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 1. AllowSimulations\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets a value indicating whether the dialog box allows graphics device interface (GDI) font simulations.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 2. AllowVectorFonts\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets a value indicating whether the dialog box allows vector font selections.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 3. AllowVerticalFonts\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets a value indicating whether the dialog box displays both vertical and horizontal fonts, or only horizontal fonts.\par
\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 19\par
\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 Properties of the FontDialog Control (cont.)\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 4 Color\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets the selected font color.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 5 FixedPitchOnly\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets a value indicating whether the dialog box allows only the selection of fixed-pitch fonts.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 6 Font\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets the selected font.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 7 FontMustExist\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets a value indicating whether the dialog box specifies an error condition if the user attempts to select a font or style that does not exist.\par
\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 20\par
\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 Properties of the FontDialog Control (cont.)\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 8. MaxSize\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets the maximum point size a user can select.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 9. MinSize\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets the minimum point size a user can select.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 10. ScriptsOnly\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets a value indicating whether the dialog box allows selection of fonts for all non-OEM and Symbol character sets, as well as the ANSI character set.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 11. ShowApply\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets a value indicating whether the dialog box contains an Apply button.\par
\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 21\par
\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 Properties of the FontDialog Control (cont.)\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 12. ShowColor\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets a value indicating whether the dialog box displays the color choice.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 13. ShowEffects\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets a value indicating whether the dialog box contains controls that allow the user to specify strikethrough, underline, and text color options.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 14. ShowHelp\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets a value indicating whether the dialog box displays a Help button.\par
\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 22\par
\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 Methods of the FontDialog Control\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab The following are some of the commonly used methods of the FontDialog control:\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab S.N Method Name & Description\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 1. Reset\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Resets all options to their default values.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 2. RunDialog\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab When overridden in a derived class, specifies a common dialog box.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 3. ShowDialog\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Runs a common dialog box with a default owner.\par
\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 23\par
\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 Events of the FontDialog Control\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab The following are some of the commonly used events of the FontDialog control:\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab S.N Event Description\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 1. Apply\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Occurs when the Apply button on the font dialog box is clicked.\par
\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 24\par
\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 VB.Net - OpenFileDialog Control\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab The OpenFileDialog control prompts the user to open a file and allows the user to select a file to open. The user can check if the file exists and then open it. The OpenFileDialog control class inherits from the abstract class FileDialog.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab If the ShowReadOnly property is set to True, then a read-only check box appears in the dialog box. You can also set the ReadOnlyChecked property to True, so that the read-only check box appears checked.\par
