\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 Properties of the OpenFileDialog Control\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab The following are some of the commonly used properties of the OpenFileDialog control:\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab S.N Property Description\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 1. AddExtension\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets a value indicating whether the dialog box automatically adds an extension to a file name if the user omits the extension.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 2. AutoUpgradeEnabled\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets a value indicating whether this FileDialog instance should automatically upgrade appearance and behavior when running on Windows Vista.\par
\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 27\par
\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 Properties of the OpenFileDialog Control (cont.)\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 3. CheckFileExists\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets a value indicating whether the dialog box displays a warning if the user specifies a file name that does not exist.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 4. CheckPathExists\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets a value indicating whether the dialog box displays a warning if the user specifies a path that does not exist.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 5. CustomPlaces\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets the custom places collection for this FileDialog instance.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 6. DefaultExt\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets the default file name extension.\par
\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 28\par
\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 Properties of the OpenFileDialog Control (cont.)\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 7. DereferenceLinks\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets a value indicating whether the dialog box returns the location of the file referenced by the shortcut or whether it returns the location of the shortcut (.lnk).\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 8. FileName\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets a string containing the file name selected in the file dialog box.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 9. FileNames\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets the file names of all selected files in the dialog box.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 10. Filter\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets the current file name filter string, which determines the choices that appear in the "Save as file type" or "Files of type" box in the dialog box.\par
\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 29\par
\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 Properties of the OpenFileDialog Control (cont.)\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 11. FilterIndex\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets the index of the filter currently selected in the file dialog box.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 12. InitialDirectory\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets the initial directory displayed by the file dialog box.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 13. Multiselect\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets a value indicating whether the dialog box allows multiple files to be selected.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 14. ReadOnlyChecked\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets a value indicating whether the read-only check box is selected.\par
\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 30\par
\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 Properties of the OpenFileDialog Control (cont.)\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 15. RestoreDirectory\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets a value indicating whether the dialog box restores the current directory before closing.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 16. SafeFileName\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets the file name and extension for the file selected in the dialog box. The file name does not include the path.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 17. SafeFileNames\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets an array of file names and extensions for all the selected files in the dialog box. The file names do not include the path.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 18. ShowHelp\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets a value indicating whether the Help button is displayed in the file dialog box.\par
\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 31\par
\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 Properties of the OpenFileDialog Control (cont.)\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 19. ShowReadOnly\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets a value indicating whether the dialog box contains a read-only check box.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 20. SupportMultiDottedExtensions\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets whether the dialog box supports displaying and saving files that have multiple file name extensions.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 21. Title\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets the file dialog box title.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 22. ValidateNames\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Gets or sets a value indicating whether the dialog box accepts only valid Win32 file names.\par
\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 32\par
\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 Methods of the OpenFileDialog Control\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab The following are some of the commonly used methods of the OpenFileDialog control:\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab S.N Method Name & Description\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 1. OpenFile\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Opens the file selected by the user, with read-only permission. The file is specified by the FileName property.\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab 2. Reset\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Resets all options to their default value.\par
\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 33\par
\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 VB.Net - SaveFileDialog Control\b0\par
